1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,997
Your AI agent searches the help docs, calls a tool, and still

2
00:00:03,997 --> 00:00:06,557
gives a customer the wrong delivery date.

3
00:00:06,617 --> 00:00:09,444
Was it the search, the prompt, or the model?

4
00:00:09,504 --> 00:00:11,331
Without a trace, you're guessing.

5
00:00:11,581 --> 00:00:14,568
Fix found: Arize Phoenix.

6
00:00:14,628 --> 00:00:17,612
Think of it as an X-ray for your AI app.

7
00:00:17,672 --> 00:00:21,263
It's free to run yourself, with almost twelve thousand GitHub

8
00:00:21,263 --> 00:00:21,815
stars.

9
00:00:22,065 --> 00:00:25,454
Add a few lines to your app, and it sends traces over

10
00:00:25,454 --> 00:00:27,595
OpenTelemetry, an open standard.

11
00:00:27,655 --> 00:00:31,445
Each request becomes a tree of steps, with timings and tokens

12
00:00:31,445 --> 00:00:32,436
for each one.

13
00:00:32,686 --> 00:00:36,890
One. Find the broken step: which documents came back, which tool

14
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:39,178
ran, and what the model was sent.

15
00:00:39,238 --> 00:00:43,061
Two. Grade the answers. Ready-made judges check for

16
00:00:43,061 --> 00:00:46,329
hallucination, correctness and tool choice.

17
00:00:46,389 --> 00:00:50,489
Three. Test a fix before you ship. Replay a traced call with a

18
00:00:50,489 --> 00:00:54,590
new prompt, or run a change over saved examples and compare it

19
00:00:54,590 --> 00:00:55,957
with the last run.

20
00:00:56,207 --> 00:00:57,795
Now, the catch.

21
00:00:57,855 --> 00:01:01,589
Its makers call it open source, but the server is under the

22
00:01:01,589 --> 00:01:05,441
Elastic License: free to self-host, but you can't offer it to

23
00:01:05,441 --> 00:01:07,278
others as a hosted service.

24
00:01:07,338 --> 00:01:11,309
Login is off by default, so switch it on before anyone else can

25
00:01:11,309 --> 00:01:15,279
reach it. For real workloads, the docs recommend Postgres and a

26
00:01:15,279 --> 00:01:16,583
persistent volume.

27
00:01:16,643 --> 00:01:19,866
And it moves fast: eight major versions this year.

28
00:01:20,116 --> 00:01:23,841
It's for developers building AI apps and agents who want tracing

29
00:01:23,841 --> 00:01:25,867
and testing on their own servers.

30
00:01:25,927 --> 00:01:29,412
If you need managed alerts and team dashboards, it's not built

31
00:01:29,412 --> 00:01:30,099
for that.

32
00:01:30,159 --> 00:01:33,449
Want an alternative? Take a look at Langfuse.

33
00:01:33,699 --> 00:01:37,811
To try it, install it with pip, run phoenix serve, and open it

34
00:01:37,811 --> 00:01:39,057
in your browser.

35
00:01:39,117 --> 00:01:42,747
What problem should we fix next? Tell us in the comments.

